  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARZ - Promotion of girls&#x2019; Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Zambezia Girls&apos; Association ( Associa&#xe7;&#xe3;o das Raparigas da Zamb&#xe9;zia) is a province-wide organization based in the city of Quelimane, with the aim of promoting and disseminating the rights of girls in schools and the community of Zambezia province. It&apos;s missionis to promote girls&apos; self-esteem, leadership and autonomy, encouraging them to promote and disseminate their rights, fight against all types of abuse and evils that affect them.
ARZ vision is a society that respects and values girls&apos; rights, promotes formal education, gender equality, and engages in girls&apos; emancipation and empowerment.
ARZ objectives is to encourage girls to report their rights in the event of violence; Dscourage the practice of child marriage at the level of Zambezia province, precisely in schools and communities, and this practice is considered to promote high cases of school dropout, early pregnancy, obstetric fistula, maternal infant mortality and the vicious cycle of the feminization of poverty and Develop school, community and school council liaison actions to increase school success.
Within this project ARZ will led the recruitment of activist, train them to led the session with girls from Nicoada district.</narrative>
  </description>
